AB  - We investigate coresets for approximating the cost with respect to median queries. In this problem, we are given a set of points $P\subset R^d$ and median queries are $\sum_p\in P ||p-c||$ for any point $c\in R^d$. Our goal is to compute a small weighted summary $S\subset P$ such that the cost of any median query is approximated within a multiplicative $(1\pm\varepsilon)$ factor. We provide matching upper and lower bounds on the number of points contained in $S$ of the order $ \Theta\left(\varepsilon^-d/(d+1)\right)$.
